{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pre-sweep against origin/main ce5795c6a5c (2026-10-31). Every figure re-derived by listing all tracked `tests/**/*.py` and testing each `_heldout` module for a same-directory base, not sampled.\n\n**Confirms the description body, corrects the title and the file impact.**\n\n1. **Count: 76, not 78.** The tree holds 164 held-out modules: 88 paired and 76 unpaired. The description already carried the corrected 76 and recorded the 88<->76 transposition; the **title** still said 78, and one sentence in the body still read \"Three of the 78 are cross-tier twins\". Both now say 76. The first comment above still says 78 in its quoted paragraph from the test-suite epic — that quote is left verbatim as the historical source, and the description governs. The 88 paired figure is independently corroborated: it is exactly 39 (361f) + 22 (19c3) + 10 (7a7a) + 17 (fb5f), the four sibling merge stories.\n\n2. **Tier split verified exactly as stated:** unit 53, interfaces 18, scripts 4, integration 1 = 76.\n\n3. **Two file-impact paths were dead and have been repointed.** `file_impact` carried `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_baseline_normalization_heldout.py` and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_identity_264f_heldout.py`, but `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` no longer exists on origin/main — the reconciler epic's rename landed and the modules live under `tests/unit/reconciler/`. Both entries matched nothing. This mattered beyond tidiness: `file_impact` is the currency basis for this ticket's plan attestation, so paths that resolve to no file are a standing source of pin drift. The description already stated the post-rename location, so only the recorded impact was stale.\n\n4. **`.test_durations` added to file impact**, as the 2026-09-07 sequencing comment on this ticket requires when claiming.\n\nDependency position confirmed: this story `depends_on` 19c3, fb5f and 7a7a, and all three `depends_on` 361f. 361f is `in_progress`, so plan review on any of them fast-fails unsigned INDETERMINATE until it closes — measured on 7a7a, which returned INDETERMINATE with `sidecar-not-emitted` rather than a verdict. No gate slot should be spent on this chain until 361f lands."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793485273971915059,"uuid":"7f888fb8-7952-49f3-9f19-cc245b550a35"}